00:59:56,700 --> 00:59:57,160
Okay.

1253
00:59:57,680 --> 01:00:01,620
And finally, immunizations.
Geriatric patients

1254
01:00:01,620 --> 01:00:04,620
should receive
immunizations like flu,

1255
01:00:05,160 --> 01:00:08,300
DTaP or an updated
tetanus toxoid,

1256
01:00:08,300 --> 01:00:10,940
varicella,
shingles or zoster

1257
01:00:10,940 --> 01:00:14,080
vaccine, pneumococcal,
and now during

1258
01:00:14,080 --> 01:00:16,420
this time, the
COVID-19 vaccine.

1259
01:00:19,440 --> 01:00:22,620
The complications of
fractures related to

1260
01:00:22,620 --> 01:00:25,680
osteoporosis are often
severe and can include

1261
01:00:25,680 --> 01:00:28,820
increased mortality,
increased morbidity

1262
01:00:28,820 --> 01:00:32,380
such as loss of
mobility, increased pain,

1263
01:00:32,420 --> 01:00:35,060
loss of independence,
increased risk for

1264
01:00:35,060 --> 01:00:37,580
future fractures,
and an increased risk

1265
01:00:37,580 --> 01:00:41,660
of having to be
transferred to a nursing

1266
01:00:41,660 --> 01:00:45,820
home or needing additional
help. So this is

1267
01:00:45,820 --> 01:00:48,920
why it's very
important to screen for

1268
01:00:48,930 --> 01:00:53,020
osteoporosis and determine
fracture risks using

1269
01:00:53,020 --> 01:00:57,000
bone density testing
and the FRAX score.

1270
01:00:57,260 --> 01:01:00,960
So bone density
testing is done

1271
01:01:00,960 --> 01:01:03,840
by x-ray. It's
imaging used to screen

1272
01:01:03,840 --> 01:01:06,500
for osteoporosis,
and it can

1273
01:01:06,500 --> 01:01:08,900
also help determine
fracture risk.

1274
01:01:08,980 --> 01:01:12,120
The x-rays are
usually two different

1275
01:01:12,120 --> 01:01:13,460
energies. That's
why it's called

1276
01:01:13,460 --> 01:01:16,550
a DEXA, a dual X
-ray absorptometry.

1277
01:01:19,170 --> 01:01:21,660
And these are just the
X-ray beams that are

1278
01:01:21,660 --> 01:01:23,760
passed through
specific bones, such as

1279
01:01:23,760 --> 01:01:27,320
the hip, the lumbar
spine, or the radius in

1280
01:01:27,320 --> 01:01:29,920
the wrist. The bone
mineral density is

1281
01:01:29,920 --> 01:01:32,700
calculated for each bone
after the person has

1282
01:01:32,700 --> 01:01:35,000
gotten this X-ray, and
then it's converted

1283
01:01:35,000 --> 01:01:37,860
into values that are
related to the average

1284
01:01:37,860 --> 01:01:41,480
female or male peak
bone mass or to the

1285
01:01:41,480 --> 01:01:43,860
bone mass relative
to the patient's age.

1286
01:01:43,860 --> 01:01:47,040
And these are called
T-scores and Z-scores.

1287
01:01:47,100 --> 01:01:50,620
T-scores and Z-score
values are usually based

1288
01:01:50,620 --> 01:01:52,480
on women, although
in some places there

1289
01:01:52,480 --> 01:01:56,080
is sufficient male data
to base it on males.

1290
01:01:56,420 --> 01:01:59,460
When that male data
is not available, we

1291
01:01:59,460 --> 01:02:02,740
use the same cutoffs
for men and women.

1292
01:02:02,800 --> 01:02:05,500
Now, the World Health
Organization and

1293
01:02:05,500 --> 01:02:07,520
the International
Society for Clinical

1294
01:02:07,520 --> 01:02:10,620
Densitometry have
defined diagnostic

1295
01:02:10,620 --> 01:02:15,220
criteria for low bone
mass namely osteopenia

1296
01:02:15,220 --> 01:02:19,040
and osteoporosis
based on the DEXA scan

1297
01:02:19,040 --> 01:02:21,420
compared with the
reference population

1298
01:02:21,840 --> 01:02:25,070
according to the World
Health Organization

1299
01:02:25,070 --> 01:02:27,940
osteoporosis is
defined based on the

1300
01:02:27,940 --> 01:02:31,340
following of bone
density values a t-score

1301
01:02:31,340 --> 01:02:33,980
within one standard
deviation plus or

1302
01:02:33,980 --> 01:02:37,200
minus one of the young
adult mean indicates

1303
01:02:37,200 --> 01:02:40,740
normal bone density.
A T-score of 1 to

1304
01:02:40,740 --> 01:02:43,640
2.5 standard deviations
below the young

1305
01:02:43,640 --> 01:02:47,520
adult mean or minus 1
to minus 2.5 standard

1306
01:02:47,520 --> 01:02:50,260
deviations indicates
low bone mass or

1307
01:02:50,260 --> 01:02:54,060
osteopenia. A T
-score of 2.5 standard

1308
01:02:54,060 --> 01:02:57,360
deviations or more below
the young adult mean

1309
01:02:57,360 --> 01:03:00,440
indicates the presence
of osteoporosis.

1310
01:03:05,640 --> 01:03:08,200
Now We'll cover
a DEXA scan every

1311
01:03:08,200 --> 01:03:10,620
other year for women
who are 65 years

1312
01:03:10,620 --> 01:03:13,440
and older, and men
who are 70 years

1313
01:03:13,440 --> 01:03:16,580
and older, or for
a younger patient

1314
01:03:16,580 --> 01:03:18,880
if they have
specific conditions.

1315
01:03:19,040 --> 01:03:20,880
Now, while
osteoporosis is

1316
01:03:20,880 --> 01:03:22,520
more prevalent in women,

1317
01:03:22,700 --> 01:03:25,390
men tend to have a
greater morbidity

1318
01:03:25,800 --> 01:03:29,160
related to
osteoporotic fractures.

1319
01:03:30,920 --> 01:03:35,360
So, who do we recommend
bone density testing

1320
01:03:35,360 --> 01:03:38,340
for? So here's a
list of specific

1321
01:03:38,340 --> 01:03:41,100
criteria. There are
others, but these are the

1322
01:03:41,100 --> 01:03:44,560
most common ones. Women
65 years or older,

1323
01:03:44,560 --> 01:03:48,360
or women who are 50
to 64 with certain

1324
01:03:48,360 --> 01:03:51,300
risk factors like
postmenopausal, not taking

1325
01:03:51,300 --> 01:03:54,940
estrogen, or someone
who is tall, over 5

1326
01:03:54,940 --> 01:04:00,000
'7", or thin, weighing
less than 125 pounds,

1327
01:04:00,000 --> 01:04:02,620
for example. Or they
have a personal and

1328
01:04:02,620 --> 01:04:04,760
maternal history of
hip fractures, where

1329
01:04:04,760 --> 01:04:06,680
they have a personal
history of smoking.

1330
01:04:07,280 --> 01:04:08,400
Additionally,

1331
01:04:08,520 --> 01:04:11,400
if they are a 70-year
-old man or a male

1332
01:04:11,400 --> 01:04:14,740
who is 50 to 69-year
-old with risk factors

1333
01:04:14,740 --> 01:04:16,820
like clinical conditions
associated with

1334
01:04:16,820 --> 01:04:19,420
bone loss such as
rheumatoid arthritis.

1335
01:04:19,860 --> 01:04:21,920
Additionally,
certain medications

1336
01:04:21,920 --> 01:04:26,400
can cause accelerated
bone loss or

1337
01:04:26,400 --> 01:04:28,360
certain chronic
medical conditions

1338
01:04:28,360 --> 01:04:30,540
such as liver disease,
kidney disease,

1339
01:04:30,540 --> 01:04:32,760
hyperthyroidism,
type 1 diabetes,

1340
01:04:33,040 --> 01:04:35,620
hyperparathyroidism,
hypogonadism,

1341
01:04:35,620 --> 01:04:37,040
and vitamin D deficiency,

1342
01:04:37,180 --> 01:04:38,740
to name a few.

1343
01:04:39,340 --> 01:04:42,100
Additionally, if a
patient's experienced a

1344
01:04:42,100 --> 01:04:44,780
fracture after very mild
trauma, it's also an

1345
01:04:44,780 --> 01:04:49,320
indication to screen,
or if it's an incidental

1346
01:04:49,320 --> 01:04:51,020
finding, for example,
they have back

1347
01:04:51,020 --> 01:04:54,300
pain and they get an x
-ray and there you see a

1348
01:04:54,300 --> 01:04:56,680
vertebral fracture that
the person was unaware

1349
01:04:56,680 --> 01:05:00,280
of, or there are
signs of osteoporosis.

1350
01:05:03,940 --> 01:05:07,800
The FRAC score is
called the Fracture Risk

1351
01:05:07,800 --> 01:05:11,060
Assessment Tool. It
was developed in 2008

1352
01:05:11,060 --> 01:05:13,200
by a team based within
the World Health

1353
01:05:13,200 --> 01:05:15,660
Organization who is
collaborating with the

1354
01:05:15,660 --> 01:05:17,960
Center for Metabolic
Bone Disease hosted

1355
01:05:17,960 --> 01:05:19,940
at the University of
Sheffield in England.

1356
01:05:20,680 --> 01:05:23,600
And basically what it
does is it generates

1357
01:05:23,600 --> 01:05:25,880
a score that is used
to determine a person's

1358
01:05:25,880 --> 01:05:28,720
10-year risk of major
osteoporotic fractures.

1359
01:05:28,720 --> 01:05:32,290
And it's calculated
based on 12 factors.

1360
01:05:32,500 --> 01:05:35,480
They're all listed
here, age, ***, weight,

1361
01:05:35,480 --> 01:05:38,140
height, prior factor,
history, et cetera.

1362
01:05:38,560 --> 01:05:42,400
The link on this
slide will take you

1363
01:05:42,400 --> 01:05:45,620
to the online
calculator for this so

1364
01:05:45,620 --> 01:05:47,220
you can test it
out if you'd like.

1365
01:05:47,480 --> 01:05:49,080
There are options.

1366
01:05:49,160 --> 01:05:51,620
One of the options is
that you have to have

1367
01:05:51,620 --> 01:05:54,100
a T-score, but on the
online calculator,

1368
01:05:54,100 --> 01:05:57,440
you can calculate the
risk if the person has

1369
01:05:57,440 --> 01:05:59,880
not yet had a bone
density and if you're

1370
01:05:59,880 --> 01:06:04,520
trying to determine
who should be treated.

1371
01:06:04,660 --> 01:06:08,460
So for patients with
osteopenia based on DEXA

1372
01:06:08,460 --> 01:06:11,560
criteria but who do not
have a prior history

1373
01:06:11,560 --> 01:06:14,580
of osteoporotic
fractures, we use this

1374
01:06:14,580 --> 01:06:17,040
calculator to help
determine the decision for

1375
01:06:17,040 --> 01:06:20,920
treatment. In patients
50 years and older

1376
01:06:20,920 --> 01:06:25,460
with osteopenia based
on DEXA criteria and who

1377
01:06:25,460 --> 01:06:27,940
have a 10-year hip
fracture probability of

1378
01:06:27,940 --> 01:06:31,680
3% or higher or a 10
-year major fracture

1379
01:06:31,680 --> 01:06:35,620
probability of 20% or
higher using this tool,

1380
01:06:35,860 --> 01:06:40,080
then we recommend
treatment for osteopenia.

1381
01:06:40,600 --> 01:06:43,960
For patients with a
fragility fracture,

1382
01:06:44,140 --> 01:06:47,480
a diagnosis of
osteoporosis based on DEXA

1383
01:06:47,480 --> 01:06:51,880
is not needed to
initiate treatment and

1384
01:06:51,880 --> 01:06:54,070
you don't need to do
the calculation here.

1385
01:06:57,660 --> 01:06:59,800
Right so here's
a summary of

1386
01:06:59,800 --> 01:07:01,720
things that
we've discussed.

1387
01:07:03,000 --> 01:07:06,700
So it's really important
to not only know

1388
01:07:06,700 --> 01:07:09,480
the effects of aging
on the human body,

1389
01:07:09,480 --> 01:07:11,860
the presentation
of illness in the

1390
01:07:11,860 --> 01:07:15,320
geriatric patient,
but also the geriatric

1391
01:07:15,320 --> 01:07:18,600
syndromes and how all
of these interplay

1392
01:07:18,600 --> 01:07:21,660
to affect the health
and well-being of

1393
01:07:21,660 --> 01:07:23,820
your patient and with
the ultimate goal

1394
01:07:23,820 --> 01:07:25,920
is that we keep our
patient independent

1395
01:07:25,920 --> 01:07:28,980
and healthy for as
long as they can be.

